      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #47490.\n\nWith DP attention + EAGLE, `--moe-a2a-backend flashinfer` on the target and a DeepEP draft (`--speculative-moe-a2a-backend deepep`), the prefill CUDA graph pads each prefill to the DP-wide bucket of the largest rank, while the draft pads only to its own bucket. The extend arm of `post_forward_mlp_sync_batch` trims the target outputs to `seq_lens_sum`, which also counts the cached prefix, so after the first prefill chunk the hidden states keep the pad rows. The draft extend then pads them to its smaller width and `_pad_inputs_to_size` fails with `RuntimeError: Trying to create tensor with negative dimension`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `ForwardBatch.post_forward_mlp_sync_batch`, extend arm: trim `next_token_logits`, `hidden_states` and `mm_input_embeds` to `_original_num_tokens` (the token count before MLP-sync padding), falling back to `seq_lens_sum` when the batch was not padded. The draft re-pads the real rows to its own bucket. This covers all spec-v2 workers, which pass the target hidden states to the draft extend unchanged.\n- `test_mlp_sync_pad_unpad.py`: a regression case (29-token chunk after a 640-token prefix, padded to a 48-token bucket, must return 29 hidden rows). It fails on main and passes with the fix.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nGLM-5.2 NVFP4 on GB300 with the 2026-10-28 SGLang nightly image plus this patch, EAGLE 3/1/4, prefill CUDA graph on, GSM8K (`few_shot_gsm8k`, 200 questions):\n\n| Topology | MoE A2A (target / draft) | GSM8K | accept len |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| DEP4 | flashinfer / deepep | 0.960 | 3.29 |\n| DEP4 | deepep / deepep (reference) | 0.920 | 3.35 |\n| DEP8 | flashinfer / deepep | 0.950 | 3.25 |\n| DEP8 | deepep / deepep (reference) | 0.905 | 3.33 |\n\nWithout the patch the flashinfer arm crashes at the first mixed-count prefill step. Re-checked on current main (`51d5502aff`, Python overlay on the same image), DEP4, GSM8K 20 questions: main crashes (`negative dimension -48` and `-32`), main + this PR passes (0.90, no errors).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo change on the default path: it only changes a slice length.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41097580594](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41097580594)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41097580593](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41097580593)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41097580456](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41097580456)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
